       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in takotsubo:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe LV dysfun w extended apical ballooning risks LV thrombus and systemic embolism; after discharge, oral anticoagulation or antiplatelet tx may be considered case by case."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " USU start 2–5 mg QD (genotype unknown) and titrate to the INR; typical maintenance 2–10 mg QD."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Interactions incl drugs that raise bleed risk, abx, antifungals, botanicals and CYP2C9/1A2/3A4 inhibitors or inducers; check the INR more often when starting or stopping any drug."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Bleed = most likely in the first mo; RF incl INR > 4.0, age ≥ 65, highly var INRs, prior GI bleed, HTN and renal impairment."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Also:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " calciphylaxis (stop warfarin); don't use as initial therapy in HIT, where limb ischemia, necrosis and gangrene have occurred."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
